The Mission: Write a program that asks the user for a specific date in three separate variables: day, month, and year (e.g., 28, 2, 2024). Your program must calculate and print the exact date of the very next day.

The Catch: You have to handle month boundaries (going from Jan 31 to Feb 1), year boundaries (Dec 31 to Jan 1), and the absolute nightmare of leap years, entirely using if, else if, and logical operators. If the user enters an impossible date (like 31, 4, 2025 or 29, 2, 2023), print "INVALID TEMPORAL COORDINATES".
